  "question": {
    "text": "In an $L C R$ circuit shown in the following figure, what will be the readings of the voltmeter across the resistor and ammeter if an a.c. source of $220 \\mathrm{~V}$ and $100 \\mathrm{~Hz}$ is connected to it as shown?\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/5y3szyU4LeOVQIVIx316mYER5fJgcnaV1oxS3xC6F8E.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "bIheh",
      "text": "\n$800 \\mathrm{~V}, 8 \\mathrm{~A}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "4MBMd",
      "text": "\n$110 \\mathrm{~V}, 1.1 \\mathrm{~A}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "OTSmF",
      "text": "\n$300 \\mathrm{~V}, 3 \\mathrm{~A}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Sfm4c",
      "text": "\n$220 \\mathrm{~V}, 2.2 \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "In case of series RLC circuit, Equation of voltage is given by\n$$\n\\mathrm{V}^2=V_R^2+\\left(V_L-V_C^2\\right)\n$$\nHere, $V=220 V ; V_L=V_C=300 \\mathrm{~V}$\n$$\n\\therefore V_R=\\sqrt{V^2}=220 \\mathrm{~V}\n$$\nCurrent $i=\\frac{V}{R}=\\frac{220}{100}=2.2 \\mathrm{~A}$",
    "image": null
  },
